{"id":"dc3dc342f45a3ac72708d0ae5281df999a6b6173","axis":"silent","repo":"nrwl/nx","sha":"dc3dc342f45a3ac72708d0ae5281df999a6b6173","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"astro-docs/src/content/docs/reference/inputs.mdoc","lines":["@@ -322,6 +322,29 @@ There's nothing to declare, and only continuous dependencies count."," A server that declares no inputs contributes its whole project, so declare inputs on servers that live at the workspace root, such as a local registry."," When a server reads the outputs of its own build dependencies, Nx hashes the task it serves once the server is running, so those outputs count too."," ","+Set `\"inputs\": false` on a `dependsOn` entry when the task needs the server running but doesn't depend on what it serves.","+For example, an `e2e` task that tests one feature of an app shouldn't rerun whenever another library bundled into the app changes:","+","+```jsonc","+// apps/myapp-e2e/project.json","+{","+  \"targets\": {","+    \"e2e\": {","+      \"dependsOn\": [","+        { \"projects\": \"myapp\", \"target\": \"serve\", \"inputs\": false },","+      ],","+    },","+  },","+}","+```","+","+The task still depends on the server, but this entry doesn't include the server's inputs in the hash.","+Nx also leaves out the servers that entry reaches, unless another entry with inputs reaches them.","+The option has no effect on dependencies that aren't continuous.","+","+Set `NX_LEGACY_AFFECTED=false` to make `nx affected` select tasks by their inputs.","+Without it, `nx affected` selects whole projects, regardless of `\"inputs\": false`.","+"," ### A subset of the root `tsconfig.json` or `tsconfig.base.json`"," "," When a root `tsconfig.json` or `tsconfig.base.json` is present, Nx will always consider parts of the file which apply to the project of a task being run."],"additions":23,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"astro-docs/src/content/docs/reference/project-configuration.mdoc","lines":["@@ -595,6 +595,8 @@ And the E2E project's `e2e` task has a dependency on the `serve` task, which ens"," }"," ```"," ","+The `e2e` task also hashes the inputs of the `serve` task it depends on. Set `\"inputs\": false` on the `dependsOn` entry to hash only the `e2e` task's own inputs. See [inputs of continuous dependencies](/docs/reference/inputs#inputs-of-continuous-dependencies).","+"," ### Ultracache"," "," Nx Cloud records the files each task reads and writes. From the reads it builds each task's Ultracache configuration, which Nx hashes the task from in place of the target's declared `inputs`. Nx still caches the target's declared `outputs`. The `ultracache` property adjusts that for a single target."],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/nx/schemas/nx-schema.json","lines":["@@ -1021,6 +1021,11 @@","                     \"description\": \"Configuration for params handling.\",","                     \"enum\": [\"ignore\", \"forward\"],","                     \"default\": \"ignore\"","+                  },","+                  \"inputs\": {","+                    \"type\": \"boolean\",","+                    \"description\": \"Set to false to keep a continuous dependency's inputs out of this target's hash and affected calculation. Has no effect on dependencies that are not continuous.\",","+                    \"default\": true","                   }","                 },","                 \"oneOf\": ["],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/nx/schemas/project-schema.json","lines":["@@ -102,6 +102,11 @@","                       \"description\": \"Configuration for params handling.\",","                       \"enum\": [\"ignore\", \"forward\"],","                       \"default\": \"ignore\"","+                    },","+                    \"inputs\": {","+                      \"type\": \"boolean\",","+                      \"description\": \"Set to false to keep a continuous dependency's inputs out of this target's hash and affected calculation. Has no effect on dependencies that are not continuous.\",","+                      \"default\": true","                     }","                   },","                   \"oneOf\": ["],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/nx/src/config/workspace-json-project-json.ts","lines":["@@ -218,6 +218,12 @@ export interface TargetDependencyConfig {","    * Whether to forward task options to the dependency target.","    */","   options?: 'ignore' | 'forward';","+","+  /**","+   * Set to `false` to keep a continuous dependency's inputs out of this","+   * target's hash. It still runs first. Has no effect on other dependencies.","+   */","+  inputs?: boolean;"," }"," "," // TODO: import the remaining variants from '../native' so the TS types stay"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/nx/src/hasher/native-task-hasher-impl.ts","lines":["@@ -220,7 +220,8 @@ function taskGraphFingerprint(","       task.target.configuration ?? '',","       (task.outputs ?? []).join(','),","       (taskGraph.dependencies[id] ?? []).join(','),","-      (taskGraph.continuousDependencies[id] ?? []).join(',')","+      (taskGraph.continuousDependencies[id] ?? []).join(','),","+      (taskGraph.continuousDependenciesWithoutInputs?.[id] ?? []).join(',')","     );","   }","   return hashArray(parts);"],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/nx/src/native/affected/tasks/dependency_closure.rs","lines":["@@ -1,8 +1,4 @@"," //! What a task depends on, directly or not, over regular and continuous edges.","-//!","-//! The planner splices a served task's reads into its consumer's plan","-//! (`collect_continuous_dependencies`), so a continuous edge carries a read","-//! like any other, and a run needs a served dependency as much as a built one."," "," use std::collections::HashSet;"," ","@@ -90,6 +86,7 @@ mod tests {","                 .collect(),","             dependencies: edges(deps),","             continuous_dependencies: edges(continuous),